        "name": null,
        "patch_url": null
      },
      "body": "`run_wrapper` calls `bitcoin_bin directly`, bypassing `node.binaries.valgrind_cmd` that `set_cmd_args` already uses. So `test_version/test_help/test_no_command/test_unrecognized` never run under valgrind, even when using the `--valgrind` passed to the test runner.\nsuggested fix for this:\n\n```\nresult = subprocess.run([*self.nodes[0].binaries.valgrind_cmd, self.nodes[0].binaries.paths.bitcoin_bin, *args],\n                        capture_output=True, text=True)\n```\n\nI verified locally unpatched, these four tests finish in ~13ms total under `--valgrind`. with this change, they take ~2.5-7s each,  in line with the other tests in this file that already go through `valgrind_cmd`.  ",
      "created_at": "2026-08-20T10:48:48Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-20T10:48:48Z",
